WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.702
A safe API should make the correct path
natural.

2
00:00:02.782 --> 00:00:05.424
Rust modules, visibility rules, ownership,
borrowing,

3
00:00:05.504 --> 00:00:09.468
and type design help developers hide
internal representation and expose controlled

4
00:00:09.548 --> 00:00:10.154
operations.

5
00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:14.197
The public interface should guide callers
toward valid use instead of requiring them

6
00:00:14.277 --> 00:00:15.984
to remember fragile internal rules.

7
00:00:16.064 --> 00:00:19.917
Encapsulation matters because invariants
are easy to break when too much internal

8
00:00:19.997 --> 00:00:20.768
state is public.

9
00:00:20.848 --> 00:00:23.986
If callers can directly change fields that
must remain consistent,

10
00:00:24.066 --> 00:00:26.598
the type's safety story depends on caller
discipline.

11
00:00:26.678 --> 00:00:30.697
A stronger design keeps representation
private and exposes methods that preserve the

12
00:00:30.777 --> 00:00:32.594
expected relationships among fields.

13
00:00:32.674 --> 00:00:35.592
A library or internal module should define
what it guarantees,

14
00:00:35.672 --> 00:00:36.938
what callers must provide,

15
00:00:37.018 --> 00:00:39.880
and what states are impossible through the
public interface.

16
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:42.107
Documentation is not only for external
users.

17
00:00:42.187 --> 00:00:45.545
It helps internal reviewers understand the
contract around ownership,

18
00:00:45.625 --> 00:00:48.048
mutation, lifetime, concurrency, error
handling,

19
00:00:48.128 --> 00:00:50.770
and any unsafe assumptions hidden behind a
safe wrapper.

20
00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.539
Safe APIs reduce the amount of code that
needs to understand low-level details.

21
00:00:54.619 --> 00:00:58.417
Reviewers can focus on module boundaries
and contracts rather than chasing every

22
00:00:58.497 --> 00:01:00.479
internal assumption across the codebase.

23
00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:04.467
When a boundary is clear, it becomes
easier to test, document, harden, and maintain.

24
00:01:04.547 --> 00:01:07.300
Memory safety by design is often API
design by another name.
